  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "It changes into a creature even if the spell is countered.",
      "oracle_id": "0d3617c3-1526-40e6-bc90-6139b5d3e1f1",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It triggers when the spell is cast, so it becomes a creature before the spell resolves. A creature that would destroy an enchantment when it enters can't be used to destroy this card, since it will no longer be an enchantment when the creature enters.",
      "oracle_id": "0d3617c3-1526-40e6-bc90-6139b5d3e1f1",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When it turns into a creature, it is no longer an enchantment.",
      "oracle_id": "0d3617c3-1526-40e6-bc90-6139b5d3e1f1",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A \"creature spell\" is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.",
      "oracle_id": "0d3617c3-1526-40e6-bc90-6139b5d3e1f1",
      "published_at": "2008-04-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn't matter how long the permanent has been a creature.",
      "oracle_id": "0d3617c3-1526-40e6-bc90-6139b5d3e1f1",
      "published_at": "2008-08-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A face-down creature spell will cause Opal Guardian's ability to trigger (if it's an enchantment).",
      "oracle_id": "b7c2c174-668d-4094-9aef-8b60c504b9b4",
      "published_at": "2006-09-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After the triggered ability resolves, Opal Guardian is no longer an enchantment.",
      "oracle_id": "b7c2c174-668d-4094-9aef-8b60c504b9b4",
      "published_at": "2006-09-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Guardian's effect doesn't wear off.",
      "oracle_id": "b7c2c174-668d-4094-9aef-8b60c504b9b4",
      "published_at": "2006-09-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn't matter how long the permanent has been a creature.",
      "oracle_id": "b7c2c174-668d-4094-9aef-8b60c504b9b4",
      "published_at": "2008-08-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It will only return if it is still on the battlefield when the triggered ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "bcc8ce61-a881-42be-ab2c-64351d17f9f8",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If one of the Theros block Gods is affected by Turn to Frog, it will be a legendary 1/1 blue Frog enchantment creature with no abilities. If it stops being a creature, perhaps because your devotion to its color(s) decreased, it will be a legendary blue enchantment with no abilities. The way continuous effects work, the God’s type-changing ability is applied before the effect that removes that ability is applied.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the affected creature gains an ability after Turn to Frog resolves, it will keep that ability.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The creature will lose all other colors and creature types, but it will retain any other card types (such as artifact) or supertypes (such as legendary) it may have.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn to Frog doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, there is no way to cast this spell to stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn to Frog overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Turn to Frog resolves will overwrite this effect.",
      "oracle_id": "74c4c1e2-c50d-4c8f-889a-0d5674dc6d67",
      "published_at": "2014-07-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won’t return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an Aura is put onto the battlefield without being cast, the Aura’s controller-to-be chooses what it will enchant as it comes back onto the battlefield. An Aura put onto the battlefield this way doesn’t target anything (so it could be attached to an opponent’s permanent with hexproof, for example), but the Aura’s enchant ability restricts what it can be attached to. If the Aura can’t legally be attached to anything, it remains in its current zone.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it’s considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners’ graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "d5b9d250-92f5-40d8-b962-4ae4adb466c8",
      "published_at": "2020-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
